{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406330-my-problem-with-necromancers","id":1406330,"title":"My problem with necromancers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-04T14:38:29-07:00","id":1406330,"title":"My problem with necromancers","content":"My problem with necromancers is that they're too cut off with the rest of vampire society. Now, on an individual level, this works; necromancy is a Discipline for corpse-fucking freaks who've decided they're going to spend months of a time doing nothing all night but play with criminal chunks until ghosts start dancing for them; That's ideal: I really, really don't want necromancers to just be wizards who took Animate Dead instead of Fireball or Tiny hut. <br /> <br /> But on a group level, they've been doing everything wrong since the Dark ages. (except the Samedi, but there are few of those) <br /> <br /> The Giovanni Tremere'd the Capadocians, who were your good, wholesome resident necromancers. But instead of replacing the Caps like the Tremere as a highly business oriented clan of necromancers, the Giovanni... tried to become obscure and retreat into their own mono-clan domains. <br /> <br /> Now, I get that they did this for their grand-stupid top-secret project, but from a business perspective, it's an idiot move. Imagine for a moment the Tremere killed the last salubri and then decided they'll go make vegas the magical capital of the world (and also take a few other cities) and leave everyone else alone? In most places, there'd be a demand for Tremere services left filled by competitors, and in vegas and such the Tremere members wouldn't get any favours because everyone else has roughly the skillset they do. That's what the Giovanni have done, and yeah maybe they have their own baronies attached to some Camarilla domains, but at that point you might as well just join the camarilla. The Giovanni are an interesting clan that has deliberately made themselves irrelevant... but also for some reason the gap they should've left open hasn't been filled by anyone else. The other necromancers are ever more obscure bloodlines and the excuse made is to keep most of them obscure is potential persecution from.. the clan who have hidden in the corner.<br /> <br /> The Hecata is just the problem aggravated; Instead of one clan that's fucked off into the corner and a bunch of competitor bloodlines that fear them, they've all fucked off into the same corner, to be even more irrelevant than before. Imagine for a moment that all the electricians in the world settled in one town; The electricians would have nobody nearby who needs their services, and the rest of the world'd be screwed when they get a power cut. That's what the necromancers have been doing. <br /> <br /> The Tremere set a wonderful precedent; They're in groups big enough that they can support eachother, but they're spread out among most cities so they all have a hungry customer base. The Capadocians failed the former, but the -should be business savvy- Giovanni failed the latter. <br /> <br /> It makes me wonder if necromancers are even needed; Just use Auspex, find fetters, and destroy them. Most of kindred society has worked just fine without corpse fuckers, why do they even exist in modern nights? (it doesn't help that I don't really know how common ghosts with world effecting powers are) Maybe once upon a time they were meant to be an edgy camarilla where people trade ghost slaves as currency... <br /> <br /> I understand some of the reasons why Necromancy is separate from Thaumaturgy, but when necromancers are treated like this, it's a silly distinction. <br /> <br /> Solutions? <br /> I kinda feel like the Capadocians were destined to be wiped out. The best solution would be to make the Samedi spread (culturally as well as in number), wind the neck in of the Nagajara so they aren't playing Dirty secrets of the black hand anymore, and set the Giovanni (and subsidiary families) up like an actual group that works with the rest of undead society whilst keeping with the corpse fucking themes: Giovanni take baronies or large domains in camarilla cities. These domains house 2-5 vampires (and a lot of mortal family members) and, unlike the Ventrue and Tremere, the Giovanni typically invest close to themselves for the sake of their mortal families. The Giovanni keep close enough with other &quot;kindred&quot; to do business but far away enough that they're not disturbed. They rarely seek trouble, but can be quite ruthless when it comes to debts. They are relatively often targets due to their uncanny ability to develop attractive domains, their frequent clash of financial interests with other clans (particularly the Ventrue), their often-low humanity, and frequent demonization of necromancy. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T15:10:07-07:00","id":1406336,"title":"","content":"I *LOVE* Necromancy!<br /> <br /> I love it so much that I gave the Brujah Necromancy as their fourth in-clan discipline in my games.<br /> <br /> That said, I agree that it's been unnecessarily cloistered away from the mainstream of vampire society.<br /> <br /> MORE NECROMANCY!!!!!!!!!!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T15:37:09-07:00","id":1406340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406330-my-problem-with-necromancers#post1406330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Giovanni Tremere'd the Capadocians, who were your good, wholesome resident necromancers. But instead of replacing the Caps like the Tremere as a highly business oriented clan of necromancers, the Giovanni... tried to become obscure and retreat into their own mono-clan domains</div> </div> </div> </div>In my games, the Giovanni is a bit different. They're an independent mercenary clan that crosses over between sects. They're one of the few non-Sabbat groups that the Sabbat respects and gives a certain level of acceptance to since the Giovanni murdered their Antideluvian. So you have Giovanni living in Sabbat territory and working together with Sabbat packs, usually on a quid pro quo basis.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile the Giovanni generally follow the Masquerade, so they've always found acceptance in Camarilla cities.<br /> <br /> The Giovanni are fairly common in the Camarilla and have traditionally served as a sort of counter to the Tremere. When vampires need magical assistance or magical muscle but don't want to involve the Tremere, they turn towards the Giovanni. They've been given the offer to join the Camarilla officially, but the Giovanni prefer their status as an independent clan, since it allows them to sell their services to a wider range of groups.<br /> <br /> Ultimately as the Giovanni are basically anywhere and everywhere and willing to work for nayone, Necromancy as a whole is a bit more common in my campaigns. Plus the Giovanni are a little bit more willing to share their knowledge of Necromancy than the Tremere are willing to share Thaumaturgy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T16:03:47-07:00","id":1406343,"title":"","content":"I think I'd do something similar to AnubisXy, except I'd keep the Sabbat and Giovanni separate. And really only because I like the idea that surviving Cappadocians flocked to the Sword of Caine for protection, and fill the slot of &quot;resident necromancers&quot; with them.<br /> <br /> Under this model, I'd use an idea I read elsewhere: Sabbat Cappadocians are hardcore survivalists, not only working to oppose Clan Giovanni, but also Cappadocius himself, whom the Cappadocians believe secretly survived his Diablerie (or faked it). They take the Feast of Folly as an object lesson, and are preparing for the worst.<br /> <br /> Indeed, given how the Giovanni would be buddy-buddy with the Camarilla, even in an independent way, I'd assume the Cappadocians would be insisting to every Sabbat vampire they can find that their Antedeluvian faked his death, and possibly even controls Clan Giovanni to this very night. After all, the Giovanni ARE extremely friendly with the <i>other</i> obvious thralls of the Antedeluvians. In any event, I'm skeptical that the Sabbat - the militant fanatics of the vampire world - would give any slack to a group that so readily deals with their ideological opponents. It's the same as with the Setites, and the Serpents of Light that joined the Sabbat against them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T16:10:09-07:00","id":1406345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406330-my-problem-with-necromancers#post1406330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Giovanni Tremere'd the Capadocians, who were your good, wholesome resident necromancers. But instead of replacing the Caps like the Tremere as a highly business oriented clan of necromancers, the Giovanni... tried to become obscure and retreat into their own mono-clan domains.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except it made them the richest clan of vampires in the world and protected them almost completely from the Jyhad.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://www.memecreator.org/static/images/templates/2101305.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T16:46:46-07:00","id":1406350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406330-my-problem-with-necromancers#post1406330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hecata is just the problem aggravated; Instead of one clan that's fucked off into the corner and a bunch of competitor bloodlines that fear them, they've all fucked off into the same corner, to be even more irrelevant than before. Imagine for a moment that all the electricians in the world settled in one town; The electricians would have nobody nearby who needs their services, and the rest of the world'd be screwed when they get a power cut. That's what the necromancers have been doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>This wasn't how I interpreted the Hecata writeup in Cults. My interpretation was that the necromancers were banding together to present a unified front, and to not undercut each other. Now they have a monopoly and can sell their services to all the sects\u2014most Camarilla cities, Anarch cities, and Sabbat cities alike will have a smallish Hecata contingent who can either accomplish what you need, or know a guy (who knows a guy etc) who can. And their reputation as the only remaining independent clan works in their favor there.<br /> <br /> In other words, it's not that every electrician moved to Venice to focus on studying electricity: it's that all the electricians worldwide agreed on unified branding and pricing (and the ones who were opposed to this idea quietly disappeared). Which is good news for the electricians (or at least the ones at the top of the hierarchy), and bad news for anyone who was relying on competition to keep prices low.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T18:29:00-07:00","id":1406363,"title":"","content":"There's always been a fairly arbitrary decision implicit in certain clans being officially not-standard. Dominate is one of the most horrific powers there is, able to Condition someone into being little more than a lobotomized robot, yet it is one of the more common disciplines. Whereas Disciplines like Necromancy, which at best equal Dominate in horror, are considered &quot;out-there&quot;, and given to clans that are sort of shunted to the side, implicitly there mainly as antagonist NPCs, or if the ST wants to Black Dog it up.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T20:23:53-07:00","id":1406371,"title":"","content":"I've liked the core concept of the clan, but I haven't liked how that potential has been developed in game (even while acknowledging the original Giovanni clanbook had many good things about it, and was probably the best of the original clanbooks). However, I have very different opinions that the OP (and likely most people on this thread).<br /> <br /> First, I like the description of Giovanni as the modern Borgias - powerful, rich, and seemingly respectable, but steeped in sin and immorality. Necromancy is just one aspect of that general immortality. (Their only ties with the criminal underworld is through the Putanesca family, a particularly deprecated family of the clan).<br /> <br /> Second, somewhere along the way, the Giovanni went from being a relatively small clan (originally described as embracing only 3 members per generation, implying on average one vampire every decade - so this is an extremely small clan) to one seemingly on par with any of the Camarilla clans (though on the low end). As a result not only were they rich, they rivaled the Ventrue. I always thought that was a mistake. In my chronicles, the Giovanni are about the size of a respectable lineage of Ventrue blood bloods who also embrace their line's descendants. Fairly influential, but nothing on par with the Ventrue or even the Toreador or Tremere. They were powerful enough not to be bothered, but not enough to risk stirring the pot.<br /> <br /> Third, what purpose do they serve in the setting? I never had major plans for the Giovanni. Although I did see them as an ultimately doomed clan whose past actions would haunt them, and they'd eventually be destroyed (as the Cappadocians were not actually destroyed as evidenced by all the various pseudo-Cappadocians out there). But that was simply their fate as opposed to what role they could play in my chronicles. So the main role they served were as the &quot;neutral&quot; Clan everyone else could deal with.<br /> <br /> Their domains were like Casablanca where Rick &amp; Sam could deal with both Major Strasser, Victor Laszlo, Captain Renault and Signor Ferrari. As such, they were a useful resource if someone needed financial help, but didn't want to go to the Ventrue; or information but were on the outs with the Nosferatu; or needed help with the occult, but didn't trust the Tremere. You'd be making a deal with the devil, but that applied with any vampire, didn't it? You're a Camarilla vampire who wants to cut a deal with the Sabbat (or an Anarch who wants a safe place to have a real discussion with a Loyalist Sabbat)? Let the Giovanni arrange it, and have them guarantee everyone's safety. The Giovanni had their own plans of course, but that typically did not involve interfering in sect conflicts. It gave me a venue to allow things that normally couldn't be done.<br /> <br /> This goes against how a lot of players expect the clan to be - arrogant vampires who thumb their noses at the other clans (I've seen this archetype a LOT in LARP). I've accepted that if I play in other people's chronicles. But this is how I prefer them to be.<br /> <br /> Fourth, while Necromancy was in-clan for the Giovanni, it didn't mean every member knew it. I always thought it was silly that any concept of the clan had one or more dots in it. No, that mob enforcer doesn't know the Discipline, nor would he ever be taught because he'd have no aptitude. Same thing with many other concepts. There were lots of necromancers within the clan of various skill, but likely half of its members didn't have it.<br /> <br /> Fifth, in terms of the Necromancy discipline itself, the main issue is how the ST wants to handle it. I never liked it as a power other people couldn't do anything about (I saw this abused heavily in LARP). So I only wanted it used if it brought all the atmosphere and perils found in Wraith. Which meant mastering a good deal with that game's lore. It meant ghosts were a prominent part of the setting, even if one usually ignored IC by most NPCs. You did get advantages from it - knowledge about the past, omens of the future, and sometimes secrets of the present. But it could also mean the Hierarchy enslaves your wraithly retainers, a Spectre burns down your haven, or dealing with a wraith who's supposedly friendly but happens to be in Catharsis at the moment. Having that Discipline meant involvement in that world.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, while they had skilled necromancers, they did not have a monopoly on that Discipline. There were skilled Sabbat who knew it as well; the canonical bloodlines had it; some Setites knew it; and there were scattered practitioners in the Camarilla as well (though not the Tremere, since Necromancy was based on the vampire's own connection to death, as opposed to the mystick power of Vitae, so Tremere thaumaturgical practice wasn't helpful to them). Not to mention all those vampires with Auspex who could possible interact with you as well. And all those mortals who had similar powers (though not as effective since they lacked that connection to death which made vampire necromancy so potent). It was its own little world that could lead to lots of interactions with other beings of the setting that a game of Vampire usually ignores.<br /> <br /> I think this crossover element is essential. Without it, Necromancy not only loses much of its great atmosphere, but most of its reason to exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":".  added a little more 08-05-2020, 02:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T22:09:05-07:00","id":1406381,"title":"","content":"I personally have to agree with Anubis, Draconis, and Black Fox.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve always seen the Giovanni as an extremely mercantile and intentionally independent clan in much the way that Switzerland is neutral. Not only to protect itself but so as to do business with both sides.<br /> <br /> The Giovanni from their inception have been in a prime position to work decently well with just about anyone. They were useful to the nascent Camarilla by simultaneously removing the increasingly concerning wildcard that Cappadocius and his clan had become while also simultaneously serving to further cement the narrative that the antediluvians are a myth - after all, loyalty to a blood god is antithetical to loyalty to a sect and its leadership. The Sabbat would no doubt be pleased to see another of the dread antediluvians fall, even if the Giovanni were not truly of Caine\u2019s line and were crass ursurers - they were still a victory and potential ally or resource. They provided a potential resource for the Anarch Movement and other Independent/Autarkis outside the sects as the Venetians would gladly do business with anyone.<br /> <br /> The Giovanni got to take a step back from the bloodshed of the jyhad and become war profiteers and one of the most financially valuable conflicts in history - not a bad deal. Furthermore their near monopoly over Necromancy placed them into a strong bargaining position with any sect and most clans. They carefully avoided being threats, taking only a few domains truly as their own and largely existing on the outside of every other sect\u2019s society. While they may not have been anyone\u2019s friend they were everyone\u2019s business partner and managed to not become as hated as the Tremere.<br /> <br /> I agree that the Giovanni should be a relatively small clan, most likely the smallest of the independent clans (prior to the Week of Nightmares) and on the low end of clan populations in general with the Giovanni family themselves actually being a minority of the clan\u2019s membership. What they lacked in numbers however they made up for with their Necromantic Monopoly, adamant neutrality, and amoral mercantile outlook. The clan was in a perfect position to accrue resources and influence, always leaning back and let the other\u2019s scoff at them for being petty guilders.<br /> <br /> An underestimation that was critical for their master plan to success, as if the other sects became aware of the clan\u2019s ultimate goal - and the potential possibility of achieving it - they would suddenly find themselves in just as precarious a position as Cappadocius and his followers.<br /> <br /> That said I also like the various Hecata groups and/or Bloodlines of Death as a reaction to the Giovanni\u2019s behavior, outlook, and monopoly. You have the mystic outlooks - many of whom potentially descended from the Clan of Death - with clear reasons to oppose the Giovanni such as the Lamiae, Samedi, remnants of the Cappadocians and arguably the Nagaraja. You have those who would naturally be vengeful such as Cappadocians, Harbingers of Skulls, Lamiae, and some Malkavians. You also have those who would simply like to undermine the clan\u2019s monopoly such as certain Tremere, Samedi, Bahari, other novice Necromancers whose business the Giovanni have a had a vested interest and quelling, and the other sects who\u2019d like a better bargaining position. However while I feel that these are all strong reasons to create a loose network of alliances to oppose the Giovanni - whether out of ideology, vengeance, or pragmatism - there\u2019s another element I feel should could be better explored.<br /> <br /> Giovanni Antitribu. The concept has been woefully under explored imo. Every clan, no matter how tightly knit and structured and indoctrinated , has outsiders. The Tremere have House Goratrix. The Ventrue and Banu Haqim both have abtitribu. The Malkavians and Nosferatu both have antitrubu, even when clan culture keeps them relatively close to the main body.<br /> <br /> It is inevitable, with the Giovanni\u2019s history and mindset, what they would generate antitribu. Even with a relatively low population and rate of embrace, antitribu are a fact of life in the jyhad. The Giovanni vassal families are scorned enough to make the notion of some Dunsirn or Milliner or Rossellini defecting very possible.<br /> <br /> These antitribu, perhaps as much if not more then the other bloodlines or Death, would have good reason to want to gather allies for support and protection from their parent clan. From this I see the possibility of a network of alliances being very useful, particularly as such a group would very much be in the best interests of the sects. I can easily see them gaining Camarilla, Sabbat, and Anarch backing alike to counter-balance the Giovanni.<br /> <br /> Anyway though, that\u2019s all just my take. Hope it was interesting for folks though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T23:32:52-07:00","id":1406390,"title":"","content":"personally i dont see the issue with the Giovannis approach - they dont want to be involed, they dont want to be in the light, they dont want to sell out their secrets. They play a different game, and that has its up and downsides. <br /> Self isolation does shield you from the jihad, persecution and laying low drs less attention from unters and other supernaturals. I might add that some branches of the order of hermes retreated entirely into astral realms for very similiar reasons.<br /> <br /> The issue i see is rather thaumaturgy - thaumaturgy is apparently without limits and can replace about any other discipline of the game with one of its paths. Including necromancy. So in my mind, the tremere filled the necromancer niche and necromancers are now just not needed anymore. You need a zombie or a ghost? the tremere have them ins tock and they are already in your city, be you sabbath or camarilla, there is antitribu everywhere.<br /> <br /> Id say if the giovanni were more,....aggressive in their presence, the Tremere would pull strings to shut them down and the Tremere have te power to do so, so laying low may be the best idea for the giovanni. Not to mention that some other clans also have their inherent issues with necromancers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T03:08:45-07:00","id":1406405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406330-my-problem-with-necromancers?p=1406350#post1406350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In other words, it's not that every electrician moved to Venice to focus on studying electricity: it's that all the electricians worldwide agreed on unified branding and pricing (and the ones who were opposed to this idea quietly disappeared). Which is good news for the electricians (or at least the ones at the top of the hierarchy), and bad news for anyone who was relying on competition to keep prices low.</div> </div> </div> </div>From a business perspective, the Hecata is stupid: <br /> <br /> -There aren't enough necromancers to really pose much competition, so you're not really getting much here. <br /> -Joining the Hecatta, for most bloodlines, guarantees the shitter. Nice city needs a necromancer: who gets the job; your rotting ass or Claudio, the boss's cousin? Shit city wants some trivial boons done? Off you go. <br /> -There aren't enough necromancers around to hunt you down when you leave; who'd notice you? What are they going to do when you're in good with the locals and they come along and try to kill a good relationship? Especially now that most guys who were powerful are dead, it should be easier to be an independent. <br /> <br /> <br /> From a game standpoint, the Hecata are stupid: <br /> <br /> -All the different bloodlines were cool, and shoving them together negates that to a degree based on opinion. <br /> -All the different discipline spreads gave us a lot to work with (I won't touch on oblivion; I don't need to) and now they're largely gone. <br /> -The death of giovanni leadership presented an opportunity to spread out the necromancers and present them as a playable clan in more games, but the writers have doubled down on putting them in the corner. <br /> -The book could've done us a huge favour and set the uprising in the present, that would've been cool, but it didn't, that all happened in the past. <br /> <br /> What did the Hecata actually do right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T04:40:08-07:00","id":1406412,"title":"","content":"In any given chronicle the Giovanni (now the Hecata) can cover 3 distinct roles:<br /> <br /> <b>Protagonists:</b> the Giovanni only chronicle where they work together against the other sects or to accomplish a goal set for them. The Giovanni families were introduced to make the clan less &quot;one-note&quot; and now the Hecata fulfill that role even better, especially if you apply the optional discipline variations between the various bloodlines.<br /> <br /> <b>Antagonists</b>: self explanatory and possibly the most common role involving the clan of death. The Giovanni/Hecata are the big bad whose plans the coterie needs to thwart in order to accomplish its goals/survive. The Giovanni/Hecata are well equipped to fill this role, they have money, power and mystical might. They might seem like outsiders to other sects but given their mercenary nature they have &quot;friends in high places&quot; (or people to compromised with them to tell them &quot;no&quot; when they ask for something) in every sect, Sabbat, and Anarchs included. So fighting them off is not just the simple matter of rallying the other vampires against the evil necromancers. As friends and allies turn their backs on the coterie paranoia sets in and the game becomes &quot;us... alone against the mob&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Contacts/Allies</b>: The idea that the Giovanni/Hecata don't work with the rest of vampiredom is just propaganda. The Giovanni have their fingers in a lot of pies. They provide goods/services to other clans and individual vampires in a similar way to what the Followers of Set do, but apparently with less strings attached. When you deal with the FoS you know you are dealing with someone who wants to hook you up untill you cannot do without their services and become their slave, while with the Giovanni most of the time they just want to be paid. Mind you, the hook is there sometimes. If they need something from you or they consider you in their debt sooner or later they will come knocking at your door to collect, but they don't want to convert you or induct you into their family. On the contrary they just want to profit from you and don't want you messing with their stuff. This role also stresses the function as mediators/mercenaries the Giovanni fulfilled since their inception. They work and sell stuff to the Camarilla, to the Sabbat, to the Anarchs and to Autharkis. In theory the Promise of 1528 should keep them out of the Jhyad but in truth they play the game as everyone else does, only even less in the open. Now that the Hacata are the only independent clan left this role is stronger than it ever was, their supposed neutrality is an asset in the way they work in the setting.<br /> <br /> It's also important to note that as a clan (well the clan heads at least) the Giovanni/Hecata had a clear goal in mind to win the war of ages and it all came to nothing because of external circumstances (the great maelstroms destroying most of their camps in the underworld). That was a thematically important element to them but one that could become the central focus of the clan or be easily ignored (when you deal with Giovanni goons shaking you down you are not usually dealing with folks desperately trying to bring up the ghostapocalypse...).<br /> <br /> That said there's a problem with the Giovanni/Hecata: because of their neutrality and it's difficult to justify having them work with other vampires in mixed coteries as they work like the Tremere clan but on steroids (because of ghosts... you never know who is spying on you). The way I dealt with this in the past was to have a PC Giovanni be an envoy to the Camarilla and another time have one pose as a member of the family supposedly estranged with his relatives. Anyway, it is possible to have Giovanni/Hecata work in a mixed coterie but it takes some effort compared to having a Toreador a Ventrue a Nosferatu and a Malkavian join forces in a Camarilla domain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":". 08-05-2020, 10:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T14:58:51-07:00","id":1406515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406330-my-problem-with-necromancers?p=1406412#post1406412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">;.<br /> <br /> <b>Contacts/Allies</b>: The idea that the Giovanni/Hecata don't work with the rest of vampiredom is just propaganda. <br /> <br /> . Anyway, it is possible to have Giovanni/Hecata work in a mixed coterie but it takes some effort compared to having a Toreador a Ventrue a Nosferatu and a Malkavian join forces in a Camarilla domain.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to say 'pick one' but you are technically correct; you can make Giovanni work with others, but it's way more effort than it should be. They work with others, but not well. The only clan more difficult to throw into a camarilla coterie is the tzmisce; The other Independent clans are far easier to work with, as are most extant bloodlines (played right, that is). Mechanically, the gio work fine. Fluff wise, they're there for an odd job or there are some weird circumstances at play. I think It'd be a lot better if we reduced the barriers here. <br /> <br /> An all-Giovanni game is slightly more interesting than most -all clan x- options. But -all one bloodline- games are good in general. <br /> An all Hecata game... That's when we get into the question of 'why?' Even with v20 rules there's only so much you can do with necromancy; one person with the sephulcre path is all you need, more is redundant. The bone path and if i recall correctly the ash path are the same in terms of redundancy whilst the other paths have little impact on the party. The weakness combination is interesting and yet the fluff is pants; a Harbringer, A milliner, a Samedi and a Najagara walk into a bar... The two corpses accuse their hookups of necrophilia and the two bad-bites eat the bartender...<br /> <br /> like, you can do it, but it's not an easy thing to keep believable. You could do a lot more with a lot less using a clan with castes or bloodlines or by using Tremere and their gargoyles...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T15:37:19-07:00","id":1406518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406330-my-problem-with-necromancers?p=1406515#post1406515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An all-Giovanni game is slightly more interesting than most -all clan x- options. But -all one bloodline- games are good in general.<br /> An all Hecata game... That's when we get into the question of 'why?' Even with v20 rules there's only so much you can do with necromancy; one person with the sephulcre path is all you need, more is redundant. The bone path and if i recall correctly the ash path are the same in terms of redundancy whilst the other paths have little impact on the party. The weakness combination is interesting and yet the fluff is pants; a Harbringer, A milliner, a Samedi and a Najagara walk into a bar... The two corpses accuse their hookups of necrophilia and the two bad-bites eat the bartender...<br /> <br /> like, you can do it, but it's not an easy thing to keep believable. You could do a lot more with a lot less using a clan with castes or bloodlines or by using Tremere and their gargoyles...</div> </div> </div> </div>If you worry about the mechanics the Hecata book gives you an optional rule to give each bloodline a different discipline spread. Also, the loresheets help quite a bit differentiating them further.<br /> <br /> As far as roleplay is concerned the various bloodlines cover different themes and areas of expertise, so a full Hecata coterie can work pretty well.<br /> <br /> And as for Giovanni working with others... like most other vampires it depends on the motivation they have to play along. Not all Giovanni need be smartasses with daddy issues and an obsession with the spirits of the dead, most of them have other interests and they might be accomplished by working with other vampires especially in places where the family is weak. Besides sometimes the Giovanni PCs really are at odds with their family (keep in mind one of the worst thorns in the Giovanni's collective side was one of them...)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T16:12:42-07:00","id":1406521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406330-my-problem-with-necromancers?p=1406515#post1406515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even with v20 rules there's only so much you can do with necromancy; one person with the sephulcre path is all you need, more is redundant. The bone path and if i recall correctly the ash path are the same in terms of redundancy whilst the other paths have little impact on the party. The weakness combination is interesting and yet the fluff is pants; a Harbringer, A milliner, a Samedi and a Najagara walk into a bar... The two corpses accuse their hookups of necrophilia and the two bad-bites eat the bartender...</div> </div> </div> </div>With V20 rules, all necromancers start on the Sepulchre path with very few exceptions, which means everyone's necromantic powerset is the same until you've invested quite a lot of xp. If you ignore that rule, though:<br /> <br /> You could have a Giovanni who deals with ghosts and the Shroud (Sepulchre, Ash, Cenotaph), a Samedi who deals with flesh and bone (Bone, Mortuus, Thanatosis), a Harbinger who does scrying and divination (Auspex and rituals), a Rossellini or Puttanesca who's not a necromancer but has a lot of Potence, a Milliner or Dunsirn who's not a necromancer but has money and influences everywhere\u2026<br /> <br /> Or you could break it up further and have one person handle the Shroud and Shadowlands, one person handle ghosts and fetters, one person handle reanimating the dead, one person handle buffing and debuffing dead flesh, and then distribute the non-necromancy aspects (influences, resources, enforcement, other disciplines) however you like.<br /> <br /> Plenty of ways to have a diverse group of necrovampires. I don't particularly love V5's implementation of necromancy (that's why I wrote my own replacement for it), but it still seems to be written in a way that's conducive to all-Hecata games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T16:23:33-07:00","id":1406524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406330-my-problem-with-necromancers?p=1406405#post1406405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a business perspective, the Hecata is stupid:<br /> <br /> -There aren't enough necromancers to really pose much competition, so you're not really getting much here.<br /> -Joining the Hecatta, for most bloodlines, guarantees the shitter. Nice city needs a necromancer: who gets the job; your rotting ass or Claudio, the boss's cousin? Shit city wants some trivial boons done? Off you go.<br /> -There aren't enough necromancers around to hunt you down when you leave; who'd notice you? What are they going to do when you're in good with the locals and they come along and try to kill a good relationship? Especially now that most guys who were powerful are dead, it should be easier to be an independent.</div> </div> </div> </div>- There were enough necromancers to have feuding factions in the past, and (notably) enough to have different bloodlines in different sects, who tried to kill each other off.<br /> - Part of the deal when the Hecata formed involved the Samedi and Harbingers getting more prestige and influence; most older Hecata are Harbingers now, with the oldest Giovanni gone.<br /> - Even if they decide to lay low to avoid the Hecata, independent necromancers are contending with the Second Inquisition without anyone having their back.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406330-my-problem-with-necromancers?p=1406405#post1406405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a game standpoint, the Hecata are stupid:<br /> <br /> -All the different bloodlines were cool, and shoving them together negates that to a degree based on opinion.<br /> -All the different discipline spreads gave us a lot to work with (I won't touch on oblivion; I don't need to) and now they're largely gone.<br /> -The death of giovanni leadership presented an opportunity to spread out the necromancers and present them as a playable clan in more games, but the writers have doubled down on putting them in the corner.<br /> -The book could've done us a huge favour and set the uprising in the present, that would've been cool, but it didn't, that all happened in the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>- The bloodlines' cultures all still exist, like how the Banu Haqim didn't suddenly lose all their lore when they joined the Cam.<br /> - The book provides different spreads for each bloodline. (It's a sidebar, and I wish it weren't, but at least it's in there.)<br /> - Except that the Hecata are explicitly working with various sects; the sample Hecata-based chronicle in the back of the book takes place in a Camarilla-controlled city.<br /> - Don't most VtM books set major events in the past? The only real exceptions I can think of (setting world-changing events in the present so players can mess with them) are the Lasombra defection and Gehenna itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T19:38:29-07:00","id":1406560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406330-my-problem-with-necromancers?p=1406524#post1406524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> - There were enough necromancers to have feuding factions in the past, and (notably) enough to have different bloodlines in different sects, who tried to kill each other off.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>This is kind of a misnomer though, it doesn't take many Vampires to make up a small group that wants to kill another group. The Warrior Salout who were miniscule in number wanted to Kill all of the Tremere... The Tremere wanted to wipe out the rest of the Salout of which caniocally of the Healer faction there's supposed to only be 7 to 8..<br /> <br /> The Old Clan Tzimice and True Brujah are very small in number as well, but still feud with their respective parent Clan..<br /> <br /> All it seemed to take to make a feuding &quot;faction&quot; in Vampire was more than one Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T22:07:13-07:00","id":1406580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orphan81</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406330-my-problem-with-necromancers?p=1406560#post1406560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Old Clan Tzimice and True Brujah are very small in number as well, but still feud with their respective parent Clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both have at least a somewhat believable claim to BEING the parent clan that the majority of the young whippersnappers rebelled against.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T00:26:53-07:00","id":1406591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406330-my-problem-with-necromancers?p=1406518#post1406518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you worry about the mechanics the Hecata book gives you an optional rule to give each bloodline a different discipline spread. Also, the loresheets help quite a bit differentiating them further.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oblivion<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As far as roleplay is concerned the various bloodlines cover different themes and areas of expertise, so a full Hecata coterie can work pretty well. </div> </div> </div>That's not the point though. Good players can make any combination work. (though if you want a quite serious game, I'd disagree with you here; It works fine if want a more comedic game)<br /> <br /> The point is that the Giovanni, the bloodlines that are afraid of the Giovanni, and the Hecata don't play well with others, or they're rare bloodlines that most ST's aren't keen on allowing and sometimes don't know how to implement properly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 08-06-2020, 03:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T02:46:08-07:00","id":1406601,"title":"","content":"I took the view of the Giovanni and the Pact they made with the Camarilla basically on the view that they were aware they couldn't pull a Tremere. The Tremere fought EVERYONE and EVERYTHING in order to become accepted as a Clan.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.redd.it/tki17gy9uoa41.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> The Giovanni saw the Omen War, Sabbat Crusades, Assamite wars, and so on and just went, &quot;Nope!&quot; They took the option of making a private deal with the Camarilla to allow them to commit genocide against the Cappadocians and went about their merry business. They decided to stay under the radar and focus on their outlandish plan to DESTROY REALITY. It makes sense because of the irony that I feel is often ignored: Augustus Giovanni is in direct control of the clan.<br /> <br /> Everyone is 100% onboard with the &quot;Endless Night&quot; thing because Augustus has Dominate as one of his powers and even if anyone wanted to rebel, they couldn't.<br /> <br /> Right up until their failure to kill Japeth bit them in the ass. I.e. one of the few beings that CAN resist an Antediluvian's mind-control (at least a tiny weak one).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T03:59:05-07:00","id":1406607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406330-my-problem-with-necromancers?p=1406601#post1406601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They decided to stay under the radar and focus on their outlandish plan to DESTROY REALITY. It makes sense because of the irony that I feel is often ignored: Augustus Giovanni is in direct control of the clan.<br /> <br /> Everyone is 100% onboard with the &amp;quot;Endless Night&amp;quot; thing because Augustus has Dominate as one of his powers and even if anyone wanted to rebel, they couldn't.<br /> <br /> Right up until their failure to kill Japeth bit them in the ass. I.e. one of the few beings that CAN resist an Antediluvian's mind-control (at least a tiny weak one).</div> </div> </div> </div>A few notes:<br /> <br /> 1.The endless night\u2019s purpose was not to destroy reality per se but rather to put the Giovanni in charge of reality. Big difference. The fact that the ritual could actually cause the end of reality was besides the intention of those who tried to enact it.<br /> <br /> 2.Not everyone was on board with the ritual. And obviously not everyone was dominated.<br /> <br /> 3.Japeth\u2019s diablerie failed but he was killed and turned into a wraith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T04:54:25-07:00","id":1406611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406330-my-problem-with-necromancers?p=1406607#post1406607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A few notes:<br /> <br /> 1.The endless night\u2019s purpose was not to destroy reality per se but rather to put the Giovanni in charge of reality. Big difference. The fact that the ritual could actually cause the end of reality was besides the intention of those who tried to enact it.<br /> <br /> 2.Not everyone was on board with the ritual. And obviously not everyone was dominated.<br /> <br /> 3.Japeth\u2019s diablerie failed but he was killed and turned into a wraith.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. It's an academic difference when the Realm of the Dead and Living are merged. The dead will rule the living [who may not exist]<br /> <br /> 2. Mind you, Augustus had almost as good a control as the Tremere did with the Blood Bond.<br /> <br /> 3. Eh, the Loresheets confirm Augustus was killed. I'm actually pleased by this as it prevents any real ambiguity.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T05:46:43-07:00","id":1406618,"title":"","content":"Augustus was a weird boy. On one hand I appreciate that he ate an antedeluvian and didn't get all the normal fakeout possession bullshit of his millenium contemporaries (Tremere deserved better) on the otherhand, an actual third gen walking around, even one that's just a glorified elder who'd be lucky to be considered a Methuselah, doesn't really mesh well with the Gehenna myth vampires are supposed to believe in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T05:54:37-07:00","id":1406619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406330-my-problem-with-necromancers?p=1406618#post1406618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Augustus was a weird boy. On one hand I appreciate that he ate an antedeluvian and didn't get all the normal fakeout possession bullshit of his millenium contemporaries (Tremere deserved better) on the otherhand, an actual third gen walking around, even one that's just a glorified elder who'd be lucky to be considered a Methuselah, doesn't really mesh well with the Gehenna myth vampires are supposed to believe in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the Inner Council knows the Antediluvians are real as does everyone who dates back to the Dark Ages and probably earlier. The idea they don't exist is just Camarilla propaganda that is mostly impressive due to the sheer brass balls of the lie.<br /> <br /> Its the equivalent of Boomers insisting World War 2 didn't happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T06:54:29-07:00","id":1406627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Legendre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406330-my-problem-with-necromancers?p=1406336#post1406336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I *LOVE* Necromancy!<br /> <br /> I love it so much that I gave the Brujah Necromancy as their fourth in-clan discipline in my games.<br /> <br /> That said, I agree that it's been unnecessarily cloistered away from the mainstream of vampire society.<br /> <br /> MORE NECROMANCY!!!!!!!!!!</div> </div> </div> </div>If you would give Necromancy to the Brujah, what forth in-clan discipline would you give to the Gangrel?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T07:00:36-07:00","id":1406629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406330-my-problem-with-necromancers?p=1406619#post1406619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well the Inner Council knows the Antediluvians are real as does everyone who dates back to the Dark Ages and probably earlier. The idea they don't exist is just Camarilla propaganda that is mostly impressive due to the sheer brass balls of the lie.<br /> <br /> Its the equivalent of Boomers insisting World War 2 didn't happen.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's not really what I was getting at. Few people active in the dark ages are still around. But the thing with Dark ages Antes is that, well, they didn't really do much. Their behaviour back then could hardly be conducive to the belief that they will rise and devour their children, send the world into war and darkness, and that young vampires have an absolute duty to prepare for the coming apocaylspe. You can't really have Gehenna on the horizon if everyone's aware that, when the antes just wake up, they'll go about their business and nothing will seriously change. Giovanni just walking around is like saying 'See, here's a 3rd gen, no existential threat here, when they wake up, they'll just chill like regular elder assholes. The other antes were doing the same a few hundred years ago. Nothing to worry about&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T07:16:43-07:00","id":1406632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406330-my-problem-with-necromancers?p=1406629#post1406629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's not really what I was getting at. Few people active in the dark ages are still around. But the thing with Dark ages Antes is that, well, they didn't really do much. Their behaviour back then could hardly be conducive to the belief that they will rise and devour their children, send the world into war and darkness, and that young vampires have an absolute duty to prepare for the coming apocaylspe. You can't really have Gehenna on the horizon if everyone's aware that, when the antes just wake up, they'll go about their business and nothing will seriously change. Giovanni just walking around is like saying 'See, here's a 3rd gen, no existential threat here, when they wake up, they'll just chill like regular elder assholes. The other antes were doing the same a few hundred years ago. Nothing to worry about&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree because I imagine they devour plenty of their children every time they awake. It's just one time they're going to awaken as complete nutters and not be able to stop feeding.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T10:29:07-07:00","id":1406646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406330-my-problem-with-necromancers?p=1406629#post1406629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's not really what I was getting at. Few people active in the dark ages are still around. But the thing with Dark ages Antes is that, well, they didn't really do much. Their behaviour back then could hardly be conducive to the belief that they will rise and devour their children, send the world into war and darkness, and that young vampires have an absolute duty to prepare for the coming apocaylspe. You can't really have Gehenna on the horizon if everyone's aware that, when the antes just wake up, they'll go about their business and nothing will seriously change. Giovanni just walking around is like saying 'See, here's a 3rd gen, no existential threat here, when they wake up, they'll just chill like regular elder assholes. The other antes were doing the same a few hundred years ago. Nothing to worry about&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Their known plans didn't succeed, or at least didn't come to fruition, yet. Cappadocius wiped out most of his clan and was trying to diablerize god. It's actually probably a good thing Augustus put the bite on him and prevented some type of Gehenna scenario, although he had his own long game for another type of Gehenna scenario. The whole Tremere/Saulot thing could be a long game and it sparked off the wiping out of most of the Salubri, a huge war between the new Tremere and the Tzimisce. As far as we know, most of the Antes were inactive, but who's to say they aren't playing some hidden long game and some of them were active through the dark ages and even into modern nights? The Tzimisce and Lasombra Antes had plans during the dark ages, too and Tzimisce hijacked the anarch revolt to fake his own death. Lasombra may have done the same to hide out in the abyss. Maybe if Ventrue was still alive/active, he was manipulating Hardestadt into creating the Cam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T13:40:21-07:00","id":1406665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406330-my-problem-with-necromancers?p=1406629#post1406629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not really what I was getting at. Few people active in the dark ages are still around. But the thing with Dark ages Antes is that, well, they didn't really do much. Their behaviour back then could hardly be conducive to the belief that they will rise and devour their children, send the world into war and darkness, and that young vampires have an absolute duty to prepare for the coming apocaylspe. You can't really have Gehenna on the horizon if everyone's aware that, when the antes just wake up, they'll go about their business and nothing will seriously change. Giovanni just walking around is like saying 'See, here's a 3rd gen, no existential threat here, when they wake up, they'll just chill like regular elder assholes. The other antes were doing the same a few hundred years ago. Nothing to worry about&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not wrong. Most of the vampires in the Camarilla officially wrote off Gehenna is absurd, either because the Antideluvians didn't exist, or because if they did exist they weren't going to go around eating everybody. It was the Sabbat that were convinced it was going to be the end of the world but most of them were written off as nutters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T14:45:51-07:00","id":1406675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406330-my-problem-with-necromancers?p=1406629#post1406629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the thing with Dark ages Antes is that, well, they didn't really do much. Their behavior back then could hardly be conducive to the belief that they will rise and devour their children, send the world into war and darkness, and that young vampires have an absolute duty to prepare for the coming apocalypse. You can't really have Gehenna on the horizon if everyone's aware that, when the antes just wake up, they'll go about their business and nothing will seriously change.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's always been a problem with the game's setting, especially when they introduced the Dark Ages setting and we got more details of the period. Certainly having so many antedeluvians seemingly die in a few centuries (Saulot, Cappadocious, Lasombra, Tzimisce - although we the players know more troublesome details about this than any real character), and the lack of any seeming threat when they (and perhaps others) were active, undercut this. And it's a big problem because not only is one sect motivated by this, it is supposed to be a subject of paranoia everywhere.<br /> <br /> So in my own chronicles, I've made adjustments that I think address this. It works for me. Sharing this out of possible interest to others.<br /> <br /> First, I heavily restrict any post-common era fourth generation vampires.<ul><li>Neither Gratiano or Montano were of the fourth generation, but fifth. And their sire (known only as &quot;the founder's favorite&quot;) told them that he had received instructions from the founder to do so, but their sire mysteriously vanished after their accounting.</li> <li>Augustus was supposedly of the fourth generation, but only because of a &quot;cold embrace&quot; where once again a mysterious Methusaleh proxy sired Augustus on the founder's behalf. So there is real confusion here in the general population as to the truth.</li> <li>Neither Saulot nor Tzimisce were known to have sired any new childer since well before the Classical era.</li> </ul>Second, I made it clear that the supposed destruction and diablerie of any of these founders is controversial in all sects. There are many that doubt these stories ever happened because there is no proof that the supposed diablerists ever found the antedeluvian bodies. Not only does the Camarilla scoff at any claims that &quot;Lasombra&quot; and &quot;Tzimisce&quot; were slain, even in the Sabbat there are many that question this. Some think it was mere propaganda, useful at the time, but not credible. They don't speak up much. But another group thinks that the slayings of these two antedeluvians not only didn't happen, but are merely a claim provided in order to justify Lasombra and Tzimisce control/domination of the sect. At most, they killed some Methusaleh. This is openly spoken by many Loyalists and the leadership of both the Brujah Anti-tribu and Ventrue Anti-tribu. Then there is a smaller group which believes in a conspiracy that is actually close to the truth - the antedeluvians may have been found, but they were not destroyed. This is a popular, but spoken only in hushes, conspiracy theory, even if only a very few believe it.<br /> <br /> The only true &quot;we killed him&quot; antedeluvian was Saulot. Meaning other vampires actually had proof the body was destroyed.<ul><li>The Tremere absolutely knew they got him, and this claim was popularly believed at the time (for various reasons if I ever need to invent them for PCs). (In modern nights, this is often disputed because of the debate over the existence/activities of the antedeluvians, but it is a pedigree that is at least claimed). Although there have always been those who scoffed at it (though they do accept at least a powerful, ancient Methusaleh must have been killed).</li> <li>The only survivor of the attack of Tzimisce of course, was Lugoj. All everyone else truly knows is that many Tzimisce went into some underground hole, and none came out except Lugoj who refuses to provide many details and has the reputation as a coward and liar.</li> <li>There is persistent rumor that the Lasombra anarchs who attacked the Castle of Shadows that they found only an empty tomb of darkness. While both claims of the destruction of the antedeluvian's destruction became vital Anarch propaganda, both have always been disputed even by their own side.</li> <li>Augustus' claim to destroying Cappadocious is undermined by vastly changed stories of the reasons and events. Part of this has to do with the nature of the Black Death, the general confusion concerning the Cappadocians during the years of the plague, and initial portrayal/claims of the Giovanni as &quot;Cappadocian Anarchs&quot; when it supposedly occurred in 1444, and the story told after the Giovanni became &quot;neutral&quot; in 1528. The diablerie is accepted &quot;fact&quot; among the Giovanni, but the Camarilla vampires discount it and it is another reason they look down on the Devil Kindred.</li> </ul>Third, I say that there is only one antedeluvian which was &quot;popularly&quot; accepted to have been active in historical times (other than the Setites claims about their founder) - Cappadocious. And the only time it's been confirmed he woke, it was always at a time of a great plague. The Antonine Plague (165-180), the Plague of Justinian (541-549), and the Black Death (1346-1353). It was during the Antonine Plague that Cappadocious supposedly awakened and converted to Christianity - news that shocked the vampiric world when rumors first spread. It was during the Plague of Justinian that vast numbers of Cappadocians mysteriously disappeared and stories of the Feast of Folly were first heard. And the last apparent rising of Cappadocious took place during the Black Death, and I used old first edition lore that the disease also shockingly infected and killed some vampires as well. So the coincidence of Cappadocious being active with these terrible plagues helped spread a lot of panic about Gehenna, and it also helped explain why the other clans looked the other way when the Giovanni began a purge of the Cappadocians (there was an ongoing belief that many Cappadocian vampires themselves spread the plague/infected others while being immune, but there are other stories which contradict this). But not everyone believes, thinking many of the stories about Cappadocious to be fairy tale stories. But those who think it is true, shudder at what might happen should other antedeluvians arise.<br /> <br /> So there is deniability of any active role of the other antedeluvians so we don't have non-threatening examples of them, massive dispute that they were relatively easy to kill, and the only &quot;reputable&quot; accounts of an active antedeluvian are associated with lots of bad things. I think this creates a different impression of the antedeluvians than canonical depiction, and one that better fits the mood the game was trying to create. It may not work for your games, but I find it useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":".  typos 08-09-2020, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T15:55:21-07:00","id":1406681,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> I did things differently. In my games some antediluvians were active during the middle ages although not easily approachable by other vampires. Lasombra was in Castel D'ombro, Cappadocius was in Kaymakli, Saulot was... biding his time inside Tremere's soul. No one really knew where Tzimisce was aside from Yorak and the Dracon. Malkav had already left Arcadia and was perfectioning what would later become the madness network. The rest was in torpor although I must mention in my games Troile is the 4th generation progenitor of the &quot;True Brujah&quot; while the original Brujah ante was asleep under mount Olympus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T16:14:00-07:00","id":1406683,"title":"","content":"So the loresheet confirms Agustus Giovanni was killed? It's not left vague, i.e. up to the Storyteller?<br /> <br /> /Sigh<br /> <br /> That's one loresheet I'm not at all enthused about. Not much to look forward to if you actually liked the Giovanni. Or, as MyWifeIsScary pointed out, any of the other Necromantic bloodlines, as they're now all collectively shoved into a corner instead of proliferating.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T16:28:31-07:00","id":1406685,"title":"","content":"It really seems the whole idea behind the Hecata was to do what the general theme of 5th edition seems to be which is &quot;Simplification&quot;. Rather than having many disparate Bloodlines and Clans which have Necromancy, now we just have one uber clan which represents the Vampire as &quot;master of death&quot;. As it's been stated we have less and less Independent Clans in the 5th edition setting, I don't really understand why the Hecata are even independent. I think they'd make more sense just fully joining the Camarilla with everyone else at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T16:53:54-07:00","id":1406692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406330-my-problem-with-necromancers?p=1406683#post1406683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the loresheet confirms Agustus Giovanni was killed? It's not left vague, i.e. up to the Storyteller?<br /> <br /> /Sigh<br /> <br /> That's one loresheet I'm not at all enthused about. Not much to look forward to if you actually liked the Giovanni. Or, as MyWifeIsScary pointed out, any of the other Necromantic bloodlines, as they're now all collectively shoved into a corner instead of proliferating.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is true but it's also true the rest of the book makes a point to leave the fate of Augustus open with several theories presented as possible.<br /> <br /> That said I think loresheets should be taken with a grain of salt. For example the whole &quot;Theo Bell killed Hardestadt but he acts as a trusted mediator between the Anarchs and the Camarilla&quot; comes from a loresheet. The information they provide doesn't always seem 100% reliable. Also CotBG has not been released yet, so the information we have might change with the final release.<br /> <br /> Edit: strangely enough, in my Chronicle of Ages the PCs killed Augustus by unleashing a few millions spectres and wraiths on him in the underworld (he was syphoning power from all those imprisoned souls and was absolutely untochable... what he did not know was that Ambrogino Giovanni had told the PCs how to unravel the wards holding the spirits imprisoned...), which fits very well with what happened to the Hecata after his disappearance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":". 08-06-2020, 07:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T17:03:09-07:00","id":1406697,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> <br /> <br /> I think the problem with that argument is that the entire basis of the Sabbat is the belief that the Antediluvians can be slain if you rise up against them. The reason the Lasombra have folded like a deck of cards and defected to the Camarilla is the realization by its Elders that they took a shot at the devil and missed. Its the realization that their entire war against the Ancients is a hopeless one and they're next in line for eating.<br /> <br /> So best to join their minions (the Camarilla).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T17:20:33-07:00","id":1406701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406330-my-problem-with-necromancers?p=1406697#post1406697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a><br /> <br /> I think the problem with that argument is that the entire basis of the Sabbat is the belief that the Antediluvians can be slain if you rise up against them. The reason the Lasombra have folded like a deck of cards and defected to the Camarilla is the realization by its Elders that they took a shot at the devil and missed. Its the realization that their entire war against the Ancients is a hopeless one and they're next in line for eating.<br /> <br /> So best to join their minions (the Camarilla).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not convinced of this argument. The vampires of the current era actually KNOW the antediluvians can be killed. Ravnos was killed (by mortals!) and that's pretty widely known so the Sabbat vampires actually know they have a chance at taking down the eldest of their lines.<br /> <br /> Also, as far as Lasombra is concerned no one save perhaps Montano knows what really happened to him. Those who were in a position to know where dominated into believing a lie and according to CbN it's actually possible that Lasombra returned on the material plane already.<br /> <br /> No. In my opinion the Amici Noctis (and roughly half the Lasombra clan with them) left the Sabbat because they were in that sect for the political power it granted them and the Gehenna crusade threatened to reduce it all to nothing. That's why they swallowed their pride and joined the hated creation of their main rivals rather than staying aboard a sinking ship like the Sabbat had become.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T17:24:43-07:00","id":1406702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406330-my-problem-with-necromancers?p=1406701#post1406701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not convinced of this argument. The vampires of the current era actually KNOW the antediluvians can be killed. Ravnos was killed (by mortals!) and that's pretty widely known so the Sabbat vampires actually know they have a chance at taking down the eldest of their lines.<br /> <br /> Also, as far as Lasombra is concerned no one save perhaps Montano knows what really happened to him. Those who were in a position to know where dominated into believing a lie and according to CbN it's actually possible that Lasombra returned on the material plane already.<br /> <br /> No. In my opinion the Amici Noctis (and roughly half the Lasombra clan with them) left the Sabbat because they were in that sect for the political power it granted them and the Gehenna crusade threatened to reduce it all to nothing. That's why they swallowed their pride and joined the hated creation of their main rivals rather than staying aboard a sinking ship like the Sabbat had become.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhhhh, that's a bit like saying, &quot;No one KNOWS if the moon landing was real. It could be a hoax.&quot; We the audience know that Lasombra faked it but given Lasombra isn't out directly ruling like he did for millennia before, they assume it's correct.<br /> <br /> No one expected Lasombra to go Darth Bane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T17:45:10-07:00","id":1406708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406330-my-problem-with-necromancers?p=1406697#post1406697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[USER=&quot;3046&quot;]I think the problem with that argument is that the entire basis of the Sabbat is the belief that the Antediluvians can be slain if you rise up against them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's a problem. Certainly some Sabbat do think they killed Antedeluvians, and/or that they can be killed easily. It's just not all. Others think the antedeluvians can be killed, but it's much harder and gauge the Sabbat at various degrees of capability at being able to do so. And some remember the Anarch Revolt was never about the antedeluvians, and resent certain Sabbat's claims about it since it's just a pretext for turning the sect authoritarian instead of remaining true to its original aims.<br /> <br /> There's room for lots of opinions about the antedeluvians, even in the Sabbat. Although I do think overall at this point in time, that the &quot;official&quot; view of the Sabbat leadership is that the antedeluvians exist and a threat, but the sect can kill them.<br /> <br /> The issue isn't making one thing right or wrong, but having enough mystery so that any debating side can be seen as equally legitimate.<br /> <br /> No, the antedeluvians do not exist, or are all dead. In any case, they are not a threat.<br /> Yes, the antedeluvians exist. They are a threat, but we can kill them.<br /> Yes, the antedeluvians exist. And we can do little about them. Once Gehenna arrives, God help us.<br /> <br /> These are all existing claims in the setting. They are all mutually exclusive. Whatever the ST decides is actually correct in his own chronicles, I think it's best if the way the setting is presented IC, that players think each side could plausibly be correct. There shouldn't be enough information in anyone's specific chronicles that the players know which is correct (unless the point of that chronicle is for the PCs to discover the truth for themselves).<br /> <br /> That's my preference and is how I run my games. Although every ST and player will have their own preferences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T02:39:26-07:00","id":1406734,"title":"","content":"I had a big ass post<br /> Unfortunately, someone knocked my computer and it restarted. So I'll give the abridged version<br /> <br /> -The Tremere became more accessible in V5; you can play them in any sect and might have a good bit of leniancy as to your paradigm. The Hecata went the other direction; More bloodlines shoved in the naughty corner for necromancer-only games. They are less accessible, and because of such, it is less simple to play them. So whilst on the outside it might seem nice to &quot;simplify&quot; the Hecata, really all they've done is make them more difficult to actually use from at least a player perspective. The Bloodlines that formed the Hecata would have benefited more from a -breaking of the house- split.<br /> <br /> -From a story perspective, Augustus putting the Clan in the corner made sense, but he didn't need to do it to the degree he did, and the degree he did it to harms gameplay.<br /> <br /> -My ideal; Necromancers shouldn't have big clans; Much of necromancy has no real place in the modern era (the physical half of it absolutely renders the masquerade), and it is quite a solitary practice. and so it would be better if instead, Necromancers were a collection of Bloodlines, none of which is significantly more powerful than any other (Samedi and &quot;The Bankers&quot; are quite large, Flesh eaters and Capadocian survivors remain small but are likely to band together should the Bankers repeat their Capadocian cull.) These bloodlines tend to look to larger clans for patronage and representation: Clan Nosferatu is by far the biggest backer (most Necromancers are gutter pariahs after all), followed by Ventrue and Tzmisce. The Toreador in particular don't like necromancers and mock any among their number who patronizes them (Ironically, this leads to them needing such services often)<br /> <br /> (This assumes that, after the Giovanni wiped out the Capadocians, the other clans put the boot on their face. If we want this to be more 'canonical' then we can assume the Hecata will fall apart, as it reasonably should, and usher in this new age of necromancy)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 08-07-2020, 05:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T06:15:31-07:00","id":1406751,"title":"","content":"I don't think of the Hecata as a Clan. I think the Hecata are a Sect.<br /> <br /> Well, technically a Blood Cult.<br /> <br /> But that's because it has two Clans that are too small to be Clans on their own (The Cappadocians and Giovanni).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T03:32:29-07:00","id":1406931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406330-my-problem-with-necromancers?p=1406702#post1406702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ehhhhh, that's a bit like saying, &quot;No one KNOWS if the moon landing was real. It could be a hoax.&quot; We the audience know that Lasombra faked it but given Lasombra isn't out directly ruling like he did for millennia before, they assume it's correct.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah. One example has video recording proof and requires a vast disbelief in not just one event, but several following events that likewise have multiple vectors to prove their veracity as factual events. The other has a small cadre of witnesses, a victim/potential victim who as with all of his age tends to disappear from historical record for long stretches of time, a victim with access to powers to allow him to disappear without a trace, and perpetrators who have all the motive in the world to claim they got the deed done.<br /> <br /> Kindred, Sabbat or otherwise, questioning [Lasombra's] demise is more akin to people questioning anyone's claims of being the killer of Jimmy Hoffa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T07:22:29-07:00","id":1406962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406330-my-problem-with-necromancers?p=1406931#post1406931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kindred, Sabbat or otherwise, questioning [Lasombra's] demise is more akin to people questioning anyone's claims of being the killer of Jimmy Hoffa.</div> </div> </div> </div>Counterpoint, if Jimmy Hoffa disappeared after a bunch of guys went into his castle where he knew he was located and killed everyone in the building, it would be a bit more credulous to believe them.<br /> <br /> The big issue with Lasombra's death is that he was living like the Council of Seven in an enormous castle covered in Stygian darkness.<br /> <br /> So it's like the Vienna attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T20:51:19-07:00","id":1407073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406330-my-problem-with-necromancers?p=1406734#post1406734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a big ass post<br /> Unfortunately, someone knocked my computer and it restarted. So I'll give the abridged version<br /> <br /> -The Tremere became more accessible in V5; you can play them in any sect and might have a good bit of leniancy as to your paradigm. The Hecata went the other direction; More bloodlines shoved in the naughty corner for necromancer-only games. They are less accessible, and because of such, it is less simple to play them. So whilst on the outside it might seem nice to &quot;simplify&quot; the Hecata, really all they've done is make them more difficult to actually use from at least a player perspective. The Bloodlines that formed the Hecata would have benefited more from a -breaking of the house- split.<br /> <br /> -From a story perspective, Augustus putting the Clan in the corner made sense, but he didn't need to do it to the degree he did, and the degree he did it to harms gameplay.<br /> <br /> -My ideal; Necromancers shouldn't have big clans; Much of necromancy has no real place in the modern era (the physical half of it absolutely renders the masquerade), and it is quite a solitary practice. and so it would be better if instead, Necromancers were a collection of Bloodlines, none of which is significantly more powerful than any other (Samedi and &quot;The Bankers&quot; are quite large, Flesh eaters and Capadocian survivors remain small but are likely to band together should the Bankers repeat their Capadocian cull.) These bloodlines tend to look to larger clans for patronage and representation: Clan Nosferatu is by far the biggest backer (most Necromancers are gutter pariahs after all), followed by Ventrue and Tzmisce. The Toreador in particular don't like necromancers and mock any among their number who patronizes them (Ironically, this leads to them needing such services often)<br /> <br /> (This assumes that, after the Giovanni wiped out the Capadocians, the other clans put the boot on their face. If we want this to be more 'canonical' then we can assume the Hecata will fall apart, as it reasonably should, and usher in this new age of necromancy)</div> </div> </div> </div>So, would you put up a different Clan for the Giovannis' spot then? Or would they still be a Clan, only a really, really small one?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T22:22:58-07:00","id":1407079,"title":"","content":"No clan. only bloodlines. Some of which are a little bigger than usual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T23:04:31-07:00","id":1407092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406330-my-problem-with-necromancers?p=1406962#post1406962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Counterpoint, if Jimmy Hoffa disappeared after a bunch of guys went into his castle where he knew he was located and killed everyone in the building, it would be a bit more credulous to believe them.<br /> <br /> The big issue with Lasombra's death is that he was living like the Council of Seven in an enormous castle covered in Stygian darkness.<br /> <br /> So it's like the Vienna attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll grant your counterpoint, but with a few addendums; Hypothetical castle-owning Jimmy Hoffa has vast power to access and utilize a shadowy pocket dimention, memory-altering powers, and who knows what else at his disposal. Lord Hoffa has survived for millennia, undoubtably facing assassination attempts during that time and having plans to avoid death that make paranoia seem tame and mundane. Oh, and of course multiple contradictory stories around how Sir James of Hoffalandia died, who was in the castle with Sire James or if there were even any guardians to begin with, and who exactly made up the attack force.<br /> <br /> The idea behind [Lasombie] and [Tzim-Tzim] dying and leading to vast change was that <i>things like this don't happen</i>. It was unheard of, unbelievable, unexpected. And we see when the unbelievable, unheard of and unexpected happen in the real world, there are people who disbelieve. In both deaths, there are contradictory stories known in-universe. And both have clan-specifc disciplines that could easily allow for a falsified death in the pre-max level range. With in-universe characters having all that information, it's hardly surprising that there would be some who question if these deaths even occurred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T01:08:10-07:00","id":1407101,"title":"","content":"putting myself in a neonate/ancillae's shoes, These are the antes I'd believe dead :<br /> OG brujah (probably) <br /> Set (probably)<br /> Saulot <br /> Cappa<br /> I'd probably believe in Augustus if it were reported. And I'd suspect Tremere dead given his silence. <br /> <br /> The others have pretty big causes to be suspicious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T17:01:27-07:00","id":1407201,"title":"","content":"Would those bloodlines be prone to one sect over the other in your hypothetical scenario? Like, the Samedi joining up with the Sabbat, both because the Harbingers are already there and the Serpents of Light share roots with them, for example, and the Bankers are pushed towards the Camarilla? Or more of a completely individualistic approach?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T23:24:19-07:00","id":1407240,"title":"","content":"Nah, everyone goes to different major sects. Perhaps as mercenaries, perhaps as loyal members. <br /> <br /> With the harbringers, there are a few thoughts to work them out: <br /> They didn't particularly care about other capadocians; it was a very lose clan. Their vengefull streak is more to do with their reduction in status from a high-clan to a deformed bloodline; cleopatra syndrome abounds. Many Harbringers likely would have fallen in Sabbat monomancy when the sect realised many of them were old and powerful. The Bankers mostly got their due, and going after them any more hurts the position of all necromancy bloodlines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T01:47:15-07:00","id":1407249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406330-my-problem-with-necromancers?p=1407101#post1407101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">putting myself in a neonate/ancillae's shoes, These are the antes I'd believe dead :<br /> OG brujah (probably) <br /> Set (probably)<br /> Saulot <br /> Cappa<br /> I'd probably believe in Augustus if it were reported. And I'd suspect Tremere dead given his silence. <br /> <br /> The others have pretty big causes to be suspicious.</div> </div> </div> </div>The average neonate/ancilla doesn\u2019t even know about antediluvians in general. Naming those who are more likely to be dead is something dedicated noddists debate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T04:12:47-07:00","id":1407262,"title":"","content":"Nonsense, give them an hour or so to discuss the subject with the right person and they'll be coming up with theories on their own. They have a hundred years to get in a good conversation. Even in the Camarilla, this isn't especially difficult so long as you frame the subject from a secular angle as a religious hypothetical with a good degree of deniability (also discuss a Setite creation myth, that's a fun one) It only becomes a problem when you start quoting from the book in earnest and proclaim the end times are coming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T23:40:29-07:00","id":1407665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gangrel44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406330-my-problem-with-necromancers?p=1406627#post1406627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you would give Necromancy to the Brujah, what forth in-clan discipline would you give to the Gangrel?</div> </div> </div> </div>I gave them something called Sharusin. It's a &quot;hunters&quot; discipline focusing on movement and tracking. They share it with the Lasombra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T06:51:55-07:00","id":1407693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406330-my-problem-with-necromancers?p=1407262#post1407262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nonsense, give them an hour or so to discuss the subject with the right person and they'll be coming up with theories on their own. They have a hundred years to get in a good conversation. Even in the Camarilla, this isn't especially difficult so long as you frame the subject from a secular angle as a religious hypothetical with a good degree of deniability (also discuss a Setite creation myth, that's a fun one) It only becomes a problem when you start quoting from the book in earnest and proclaim the end times are coming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, noddist studies are not widespread at all. Most contemporary vampires don't know and don't care about the antediluvians and don't have the time or the inclination to find out or focus themselves on quasi mythical stuff. They are too busy surviving and/or plotting, and with the so called &quot;Gehenna craze&quot;. You are of course entitled to believe the contrary but it's simply not how things are presented in VtM lore.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}